{
  "dom_id": "step-q73162",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Find the coefficient of ${x}^{4}$ in the expansion of  ${(z+2x)}^{4}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the exponent of the binomial expression is $n=4,$ we see that the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{z}^{4}{x}^{0},\\,{z}^{3}{x}^{1},\\,{z}^{2}{x}^{2},\\,{z}^{1}{x}^{3},\\,{z}^{0}{x}^{4},\n$$\n\nOf these, the term that returns ${x}^{4}$ is the fifth. So, we are looking for the fifth term in the binomial expansion.\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore, the fifth term in the binomial expansion is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1{(z)}^{0}{(2x)}^{4}=1(1)(16{x}^{4})=16{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${x}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(z+2x)}^{4}$ is $16.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
